-- title:
--   Proposition 3.12(a) — explicit deletion interval in reduced degree minus one
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be any field, $V$ a finite decidable vertex set with a rank embedding into $\mathbb N$, $K$ a finite downward-closed complex on $V$, and $f$ a real-valued face weight monotone under inclusion. Filtration levels contain faces of weight at most $t$, and persistence maps run from $t$ to $s$ for $s\le t$. Fix $i\in V$ and $\sigma\subseteq V\setminus\{i\}$, and work in cohomological degree $q=|\sigma|$. Write $\mathfrak p_i=(x_v:v\ne i)$. The original homogeneous $H^q_{\mathfrak p_i}$ persistence functor with distinguished degree $0$ and complementary degree $-\mathbf1_\sigma$ is naturally isomorphic, including all of its original quotient-induced maps, to the single interval module with the following support when $\sigma\in K$, and is zero otherwise:
--
--   $$\left[f(\sigma),\min_{\substack{v\notin\sigma\cup\{i\}\\\sigma\cup\{v\}\in K}}f(\sigma\cup\{v\})\right).$$
--
--   The minimum of an empty coface set is $+\infty$. The interval is closed at birth and open at death. If birth equals death, or the required face is absent, the support is empty and the interval module is zero. Void complexes, the complex $\{\varnothing\}$, ghost vertices and empty faces are retained.
